<h2>Questions</h2>
<h3>Can I set a website as the new tab page without an extension?</h3>
<p>
  No. Chrome has no setting for a new tab address. The Home button and the startup pages are the
  closest it gets.
</p>
<h3>Do I lose Google search on a new tab?</h3>
<p>
  The address bar still searches with your search engine, as it does on any page. In TabCabin,
  <kbd>Ctrl+K</kbd> searches your boards, open tabs and bookmarks.
</p>
<h3>How do I get Chrome's own page back?</h3>
<p>
  Turn the extension off in Manage Extensions, or remove it. With TabCabin, sign in or export a
  backup from Settings → Data first, so your boards are kept.
</p>
